 s.note('We added modules under src/ams/research rather than replacing original memory governance. Ledger/policy code is pure typed state logic with no SDK imports. Retrieval binds logical records to native claims/chunks, intersects artifact permissions and applies the chosen score/gate. Sequential state serializes graph/index, caches, chunks, RNG and evidence using explicit JSON, with ordered intents and exact saved replies; unknown call outcomes stop rather than invent exactly-once guarantees. Execution guards preserve the shared budget across restarts and settle authoritative costs; judges never write trust. The current audit passed 612 collected tests, not a sum of overlapping older test reports. All 648 static contexts and governance hashes match original retrieval using exact saved replies. These engineering checks are not proof of defense efficacy or real identity authentication. The old Phase 1 validator over-includes later research modules in a producer fingerprint; saved newer native/provisional artifacts verify, but affected regeneration/import commands need a versioned fix. Original loader/logging/transport infrastructure changes are documented in README §5. No training occurred.',[SRC.audit,SRC.retrieval,SRC.ledger,'src/ams/research/sequential/runner.py','README.md §5']);
